DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iissaallpphhaa() and iissaallpphhaa__ll() functions test for any character for which
     isupper(3), isupper_l(3) or islower(3), islower_l(3) is true.  The value
     of the argument must be representable as an _u_n_s_i_g_n_e_d _c_h_a_r or the value of
     EOF.

     In the ASCII character set, this includes the following characters (with
     their numeric values shown in octal):

     101 ``A''     102 ``B''     103 ``C''     104 ``D''     105 ``E''
     106 ``F''     107 ``G''     110 ``H''     111 ``I''     112 ``J''
     113 ``K''     114 ``L''     115 ``M''     116 ``N''     117 ``O''
     120 ``P''     121 ``Q''     122 ``R''     123 ``S''     124 ``T''
     125 ``U''     126 ``V''     127 ``W''     130 ``X''     131 ``Y''
     132 ``Z''     141 ``a''     142 ``b''     143 ``c''     144 ``d''
     145 ``e''     146 ``f''     147 ``g''     150 ``h''     151 ``i''
     152 ``j''     153 ``k''     154 ``l''     155 ``m''     156 ``n''
     157 ``o''     160 ``p''     161 ``q''     162 ``r''     163 ``s''
     164 ``t''     165 ``u''     166 ``v''     167 ``w''     170 ``x''
     171 ``y''     172 ``z''

     The iissaallpphhaa__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas the
     iissaallpphhaa() function uses the current global or per-thread locale.

